From caneff at gmail.com  Thu Mar  8 17:22:11 2012
From: caneff at gmail.com (Chris Neff)
Date: Thu, 8 Mar 2012 11:22:11 -0500
Subject: [datatable-help] problems with adding a DateTime column
In-Reply-To: <FD59D3740610AB4388AA1BDC7FC9531D5EAE7CE7@CRP11EXHMBS01.GAINCapital.com>
References: <FD59D3740610AB4388AA1BDC7FC9531D5EAE7CE7@CRP11EXHMBS01.GAINCapital.com>
Message-ID: <CAAuY0RX87dBu7Hb_BPYF3iXkxJ7gbfrzkB370b-=RyBKpHEATw@mail.gmail.com>

Try as.IDate around your strptime.  strptime returns POSIXlt which
isn't really amenable to data tables (or frames for that matter).  In
base R you would usually convert to POSIXct, but IDate is integer
based and made to be able to key on dates in data.tables.

